# Batch Rename Studio — Design Contract

This document is the authoritative internal design. Work cards (`docs/workcards/`)
implement it. Where this document and the task's "Fixed contract" disagree, the
Fixed contract wins and the deviation must be reported, not silently resolved.

## 1. Solution layout

```
BatchRenameStudio.sln                      (repo root)
src/BatchRenameStudio.Core/                net8.0 class library, no WinForms, no NuGet
    BatchRenameStudio.Core.csproj
    Rules/            RuleSet.cs, RuleStep.cs, RuleSetLoader.cs
    Engine/           NameEngine.cs, NameValidator.cs, SequencePattern.cs
    Planning/         FileEntry.cs, PlanItem.cs, RenamePlan.cs, RenamePlanner.cs, PlanSerializer.cs
    Execution/        RenameExecutor.cs, RenameHistory.cs      (added by WC-3)
src/BatchRenameStudio/                     net8.0-windows WinExe, WinForms, references Core
    BatchRenameStudio.csproj
    Program.cs
    Cli/              HeadlessRunner.cs, ConsoleBridge.cs
    Gui/              MainForm.cs, StepDialog.cs, StepText.cs   (added by WC-3)
docs/                DESIGN.md, DECISIONS.md, workcards/
README.md
```

Rationale: the whole spec-critical rule engine lives in a plain `net8.0` library
with zero UI dependencies, so it is testable from the command line and cannot be
contaminated by WinForms concerns. The `net8.0-windows` executable is a thin
shell: argument routing + GUI.

Both projects: `<Nullable>enable</Nullable>`, `<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>`,
`<LangVersion>` default. No `PackageReference` of any kind. No `global.json`.

## 2. Mandated public API of `BatchRenameStudio.Core`

Signatures below are binding: WC-2 and WC-3 are written against them. Namespaces
are as written. Additional internal/private helpers are free.

```csharp
namespace BatchRenameStudio.Core.Rules;

public enum ApplyTo  { Name, NameAndExtension }
public enum SortMode { Name, Created, Modified }

public abstract record RuleStep;
public sealed record ReplaceStep(string Find, string ReplaceWith, bool Regex, bool IgnoreCase) : RuleStep;
public sealed record InsertStep(string Text, InsertPosition Position, int Index) : RuleStep;
public sealed record RemoveStep(int From, int Count) : RuleStep;
public sealed record SequenceStep(string Pattern, int Start, int Step, AffixPosition Position) : RuleStep;
public sealed record CaseStep(CaseMode Mode) : RuleStep;
public sealed record ExtensionStep(ExtensionMode Mode, string Value) : RuleStep;

public enum InsertPosition { Prefix, Suffix, Index }
public enum AffixPosition  { Prefix, Suffix }
public enum CaseMode       { Upper, Lower, Title }
public enum ExtensionMode  { Lower, Upper, Set }

public sealed class RuleSet
{
    public ApplyTo ApplyTo { get; set; } = ApplyTo.Name;
    public SortMode Sort   { get; set; } = SortMode.Name;
    public List<RuleStep> Steps { get; } = new();
}

public sealed class RuleSetException : Exception
{
    public RuleSetException(string message) : base(message) { }
}

public static class RuleSetLoader
{
    /// <summary>Parses rules.json. Throws RuleSetException on any malformed input.</summary>
    public static RuleSet FromJson(string json);
    public static RuleSet FromFile(string path);
    /// <summary>Serializes a RuleSet back to the documented rules.json shape (GUI "Save rules").</summary>
    public static string ToJson(RuleSet rules);
}
```

```csharp
namespace BatchRenameStudio.Core.Engine;

public static class NameEngine
{
    /// <summary>Rule 2 split. Returned Ext never contains the dot.</summary>
    public static (string Base, string Ext) Split(string fileName);
    /// <summary>Rule 12 reassembly: b + "." + ext when ext is non-empty, else b.</summary>
    public static string Join(string baseName, string ext);
    /// <summary>Rule 10 title casing.</summary>
    public static string ToTitleCase(string value);
    /// <summary>Full pipeline for one file. sequenceIndex is 0-based position in processing order.</summary>
    public static string ComputeProposedName(string originalName, RuleSet rules, int sequenceIndex);
}

public static class NameValidator
{
    /// <summary>Rule 13 "invalid" test. reason is a short human string, "" when valid.</summary>
    public static bool IsInvalid(string proposedName, out string reason);
}
```

```csharp
namespace BatchRenameStudio.Core.Planning;

public enum ItemStatus { Ok, Collision, Unchanged, Invalid }

public sealed record FileEntry(string Name, DateTime CreatedUtc, DateTime ModifiedUtc);
public sealed record PlanItem(string Original, string Proposed, ItemStatus Status, string Reason);

public sealed class PlanSummary
{
    public int Total { get; init; }
    public int Ok { get; init; }
    public int Collision { get; init; }
    public int Unchanged { get; init; }
    public int Invalid { get; init; }
}

public sealed class RenamePlan
{
    public int SchemaVersion => 1;
    public IReadOnlyList<PlanItem> Items { get; }
    public PlanSummary Summary { get; }
}

public static class RenamePlanner
{
    /// <summary>Enumerates the directory (rule 1) and builds the plan.</summary>
    public static RenamePlan Create(string directory, RuleSet rules);
    /// <summary>Pure overload: caller supplies the file set. Used by the GUI and by tests.</summary>
    public static RenamePlan Create(IReadOnlyList<FileEntry> files, RuleSet rules);
    /// <summary>Rule 5 ordering, exposed so the GUI shows the same order.</summary>
    public static IReadOnlyList<FileEntry> SortFiles(IReadOnlyList<FileEntry> files, SortMode sort);
}

public static class PlanSerializer
{
    /// <summary>Deterministic JSON text: 2-space indent, LF newlines, exactly one trailing LF.</summary>
    public static string ToJson(RenamePlan plan);
    /// <summary>Writes ToJson(plan) as UTF-8 without BOM.</summary>
    public static void WriteToFile(RenamePlan plan, string path);
}
```

## 3. Semantics — implementation notes that are easy to get wrong

These restate the fixed contract at implementation level. Implement literally.

**S1 Split.** `dot = fileName.LastIndexOf('.')`. If `dot > 0`: base = `[0,dot)`,
ext = `[dot+1, end)`. Else base = whole name, ext = `""`. `.gitignore` → base
`.gitignore`, ext `""`. `a.` → dot=1>0 → base `a`, ext `""`.

**S2 Pipeline.** For one file with 0-based `sequenceIndex`:

```
(b, e) = Split(original)
target = (applyTo == Name) ? b : original
for each step in order:
    if step is ExtensionStep:
        if applyTo == Name:
            e = ApplyExtension(e, step)
        else:
            (tb, te) = Split(target)
            target = Join(tb, ApplyExtension(te, step))
    else:
        target = ApplyTextStep(target, step, sequenceIndex)
return (applyTo == Name) ? Join(target, e) : target
```

**S3 ApplyTextStep.**
- `ReplaceStep`: if `Find` is `""` → return input unchanged (guards
  `string.Replace` throwing on an empty search string). Regex mode:
  `Regex.Replace(s, Find, ReplaceWith, IgnoreCase ? RegexOptions.IgnoreCase : RegexOptions.None)`.
  Literal mode: `s.Replace(Find, ReplaceWith, IgnoreCase ? StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase : StringComparison.Ordinal)`.
- `InsertStep`: Prefix → `Text + s`; Suffix → `s + Text`; Index →
  `s.Insert(Math.Clamp(Index, 0, s.Length), Text)`.
- `RemoveStep`: `from = Math.Clamp(From, 0, s.Length)`,
  `count = Math.Clamp(Count, 0, s.Length - from)`, then `s.Remove(from, count)`.
- `SequenceStep`: `value = Start + Step * sequenceIndex` (checked in `long`, then
  cast back with saturation is NOT required — plain `int` arithmetic is fine).
  `rendered = SequencePattern.Render(Pattern, value)`. Prefix → `rendered + s`;
  Suffix → `s + rendered`.
- `CaseStep`: Upper → `ToUpperInvariant()`, Lower → `ToLowerInvariant()`,
  Title → `NameEngine.ToTitleCase`.

**S4 ApplyExtension.** Lower → `ext.ToLowerInvariant()`, Upper →
`ext.ToUpperInvariant()`, Set → `Value` verbatim (no dot-stripping, no trimming).

**S5 SequencePattern.Render.** Find the FIRST match of `\{n:(0+)\}` in the
pattern. If none, return the pattern verbatim. Otherwise width = length of the
captured zero-run and the token is replaced by
`value.ToString(new string('0', width), CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)`. Only that
first occurrence is replaced. Negative values render as `-007` style — accepted.

**S6 ToTitleCase.** Walk the string char by char; `inRun` starts false.
`char.IsLetter(c)` true → emit `inRun ? char.ToLowerInvariant(c) : char.ToUpperInvariant(c)`
and set `inRun = true`. Otherwise emit `c` unchanged and set `inRun = false`.

**S7 NameValidator.IsInvalid.** In this order, first hit wins, reason set:
`Length == 0` → "empty"; `Length > 255` → "too long"; contains any of
`< > : " / \ | ? *` or any `c < ' '` → "illegal character";
`Split(name).Base` equals (OrdinalIgnoreCase) one of `CON PRN AUX NUL COM1..COM9
LPT1..LPT9` → "reserved device name". Else false, reason `""`.

**S8 Enumeration (rule 1).** `Directory.EnumerateFiles(dir)` only; then skip any
entry whose `FileAttributes` include `Directory` or `ReparsePoint`. Hidden and
system files ARE included. Times: `File.GetCreationTimeUtc` /
`File.GetLastWriteTimeUtc`. `Path.GetFileName` supplies `FileEntry.Name`.

**S9 Sort (rule 5).** `Name` → `string.CompareOrdinal(a.Name, b.Name)`.
`Created` → `CreatedUtc` ascending, ties broken by `string.CompareOrdinal` on the
name. `Modified` → same with `ModifiedUtc`. The tie-break is what makes rule 15
(determinism) hold on filesystems with coarse timestamps. Use a stable sort
(`List.Sort` is NOT stable — use `OrderBy`/`ThenBy` or an explicit comparator that
already falls back to the name).

**S10 Status (rule 13), evaluated per item i over the sorted array:**
1. `NameValidator.IsInvalid(proposed[i])` → `Invalid`.
2. Collision if either: some `k != i` with
   `files[k].Name.Equals(proposed[i], OrdinalIgnoreCase)`, or some `k != i` with
   `proposed[k].Equals(proposed[i], OrdinalIgnoreCase)`. Items of every status,
   including `Invalid`, participate as `k`. No chain/cycle resolution: this is a
   literal reading of rule 13.
3. `proposed[i]` equals `files[i].Name` ordinally → `Unchanged`.
4. Else `Ok`.

**S11 plan.json shape.** Property names exactly `schemaVersion`, `items`,
`original`, `proposed`, `status`, `reason`, `summary`, `total`, `ok`,
`collision`, `unchanged`, `invalid`. `status` values are lowercase
`ok|collision|unchanged|invalid`. `items` is in processing order (rule 14).

**S12 Determinism (rule 15).** Serialize with `Utf8JsonWriter`
(`Indented = true`, `IndentSize` default 2,
`Encoder = JavaScriptEncoder.UnsafeRelaxedJsonEscaping`), decode the buffer as
UTF-8, replace `"\r\n"` with `"\n"`, ensure exactly one trailing `"\n"`, then
write bytes via `new UTF8Encoding(encoderShouldEmitUTF8Identifier: false)`.
Never use `Environment.NewLine`, `DateTime.Now`, or any culture-sensitive
formatting anywhere in the Core library.

## 4. CLI contract (WC-2)

`BatchRenameStudio.exe --plan --dir <folder> --rules <rules.json> --out <plan.json>`

- Flags may appear in any order. `--plan` must be present to enter headless mode.
- Exactly one line on stdout on success:
  `plan: total=N ok=N collision=N unchanged=N invalid=N`
- Nothing else on stdout, ever. All diagnostics go to stderr.
- Exit codes: `0` success; `2` bad/missing arguments; `3` directory not found;
  `4` rules file missing or unparseable; `5` failure writing the output file.
- No file in `<folder>` is created, renamed, or deleted in `--plan` mode. The
  `--out` file is the only write.
- With no arguments (or no `--plan`), the process starts the GUI.

## 5. GUI model (WC-3)

Single window, code-built controls only (no `.Designer.cs`, no `.resx`).
Live preview: any change to folder, sort, applyTo, or the step list recomputes
the plan through the same `RenamePlanner` the CLI uses — one engine, one truth.
Apply renames only `Ok` items, in two phases (every source first moved to a
unique temp name in the same folder, then to its target) so swaps and cycles
cannot destroy data. Every apply writes a history file; Undo replays it in
reverse. Details in `docs/workcards/WC-3-gui.md`.

